    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d485-a1">

                <pb facs="0512" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg492"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 1.</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Pruyn to the Gorogio</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 49.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States in
                                Japan</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Kanagawa</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-05-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 16, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>I have to state that I have been instructed by the President of the United States
                    to inform your excellencies that he has been pleased to approve of my resistance
                    to the extraordinary request made by you at the interview at the <pb facs="0513"
                        n="493" xml:id="pg493"/> naval school for the closing of this port, and of
                    the fidelity and frankness with which I explained my proceedings in that respect
                    to the representatives of the other treaty powers.</p>
                <p>With respect and esteem,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROBERT H. PRUYN, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the United
                            States in Japan.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Their Excellencies <hi rendition="#small-caps">Itakura Suwo-no-kami, Inowuye
                            Kawatsi-no-Kami, Makino Redzen-no-kami</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Ministers for Foreign Affairs, &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        Yedo.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
